# Technical decision log (ADRs)

Before implementing work that needs a design call, confirm with the user per [pre-implementation-decision-check](pre-implementation-decision-check.mdc).

When you make or materially change a **non-trivial** technical choice (framework, crate, schema field, export format, coordinate system, build wiring), **add or update** an entry in [`docs/decisions/`](../../docs/decisions/).

## File naming

- Pattern: `NNNN-short-kebab-title.md` under `docs/decisions/`.
- `NNNN`: four digits, **monotonic** (next unused number; do not renumber existing files).
- Prefer one decision per file; amend via a new ADR if the decision is superseded.

## Template (copy into new file)

```markdown
# <Short title>

- **Status**: proposed | accepted | superseded | deprecated
- **Date**: YYYY-MM-DD
- **Context**: What problem or constraint triggered this?
- **Decision**: What we chose, concretely.
- **Alternatives considered**: What else was evaluated and why not.
- **Consequences**: Trade-offs, follow-up work, migrations.
- **Links**: PRs, issues, related ADRs (optional).
```

Keep entries **short** (rough target: one screen). Use [Michael Nygard–style ADR](https://cognitect.com/blog/2011/11/15/documenting-architecture-decisions) framing: context → decision → consequences.

## Index

Maintain the table in [`docs/decisions/README.md`](../../docs/decisions/README.md) when adding a decision (title + file link + status).
